<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cleombrotus I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 371 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/4th-century-bce">4th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cleombrotus I was an Agiad king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a> from 380 to 371 BCE. He led several Spartan expeditions against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes-greece">Thebes</a> in the 370s, and in 371 BCE commanded the army that was defeated at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leuctra">Battle of Leuctra</a> by the Boeotians under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epaminondas">Epaminondas</a>. He was killed in the battle, and his death and the losses among the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spartiates">Spartiates</a> marked the end of Spartan supremacy.</p></div>
